notes.body:
@AndersBroman @johnthacker: Sadly zlib-ng is not available in Debian and derivatives yet. There is an already ongoing packaging effort by Guillem at https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1002056, which had an update a few weeks ago.
I think the best course of action is waiting for the official package in Debian and possibly backporting that to the PPAs.

I'm wondering how important is speeding up zlib compression/decompresion when zstd is already supported and may give better performance already (https://databento.com/blog/zstd-vs-zlib). I'm not against implementing zlib-ng support, just trying to assess if providing zlib-ng backports would be worth it.

